    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode over the city.\n\n**`Locality.java`** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/Locality.java`):\n- Added the region-to-postcode range table (`NSW 2000-2099`, `VIC 3000-3099`, `QLD 4000-4099`), matching the ranges already used in `OwnerPostcode`.\n- Changed `of(String city)` \u2192 `of(String postcode, String city)`. It first tries `byPostcode(...)`: a 4-digit postcode landing inside a known range returns that region. Only when the postcode is null, malformed, or in no known range does it fall back to the city-to-region table (still deriving `UNKNOWN` for unlisted cities).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**: updated the `locality` expression to `Locality.of(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity())`.\n\nThis returns the same region for known cities (e.g. Sydney with a NSW-range postcode \u2192 `NSW`) while disambiguating same-named cities by their actual postcode. Both acceptance tests pass \u2014 `coreRegionFromPostcodeRange` (Sydney/2000 \u2192 NSW) and `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` (unknown city + 3000 \u2192 VIC, proving postcode precedence).",
