    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the full ordered trace for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the endpoint file declares `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. A caller without that role never enters the pipeline.\n- **Single transaction** \u2014 every step carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole pipeline (including the writes to *other* owners in `AssignHousehold`) runs in one transaction that commits once at the end.\n\nThe steps then run in the exact `next:` order below.\n\n### 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` (binds `@RequestBody`, the only step that reads the body)\nValidations, in this internal order:\n1. **Required fields** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank; `address` must be non-null/non-blank *after normalization*. All offending field names are collected and, if any, \u2192 `OwnerFieldsRequiredException` \u2192 **400**.\n2. **Postcode** (only if required checks passed) \u2014 optional; if present must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in range \u2192 else `OwnerPostcodeInvalidException` \u2192 **400**. (Note: the region lookup uses the *raw* `request.getCity()`, matched case-sensitively against `\"Sydney\"/\"Melbourne\"/\"Brisbane\"`.)\n3. **Telephone** \u2014 normalized to E.164 (strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps `+CC` if given, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; 8\u201315 digits; `+61`\u21d29 national digits, `+1`\u21d210) \u2192 else `OwnerTelephoneInvalidException` \u2192 **400**.\n4. **Email** \u2014 optional; if non-blank must match the address regex \u2192 else `OwnerEmailInvalidException` \u2192 **400**.\n\nSide-effects (mutations written back onto the body): sets **normalized address**, **E.164 telephone**, **lower-cased email**, then republishes the body as an `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>` variable.\n\n### 2. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`\nComputes the effective business day (supplied `registrationDate` or `LocalDate.now()`, rolled forward off weekends). Counts existing owners with that `registrationDate`; if **\u2265 100** \u2192 `OwnerDailyLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n### 3. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`\nCounts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if **\u2265 50** \u2192 `OwnerCityCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n### 4. `BuildOwner`\nMaps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity. Defaults missing registration date to today, then rolls it forward to the next business day (weekend \u2192 Monday). Publishes `Out<Owner>`.\n\n### 5. `AssignHousehold`\nOnly if request opts in with `sharesHousehold: true` **and** an existing owner matches on last name (normalized) + address (normalized). Side-effects: sets a deterministic `householdId` (`HH-` + 12 hex of SHA-256(lastName|address)) on the new owner **and saves that id onto every existing household member** that lacks it.\n\n### 6. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`\nBuilds the new owner's `identityKey` = `telephone|email|householdId`. If any existing owner has an identical whole key \u2192 `OwnerIdentityConflictException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n### 7. `AssignHouseholdSize`\nSets `householdMemberCount` = existing members sharing `householdId` + 1 (or 1 when no household).\n\n### 8. `AssignCustomerCode`\nSets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is per-city sequence = (owners already in that city, case-insensitive) + 1.\n\n### 9. `AssignNamesakeCount`\nSets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding the new owner.\n\n### 10. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`\nSets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when existing owners for this owner's business day is **> 80**.\n\n### 11. `SaveOwner`\nPersists the new owner via `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (assigns the generated id).\n\n### 12. `AuditOwnerCreated`\nSide-effect only: writes an `AUDIT` log line with id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and the derived `MembershipLevel` (1 base, +1 if email present, +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3).\n\n### 13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\nMaps entity \u2192 `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\nTwo ordering consequences worth flagging, both visible in the code: the daily-limit and city-capacity checks run *before* the identity/duplicate check, so a duplicate request in a full city returns 409-capacity rather than 409-conflict; and because everything shares one transaction, `AssignHousehold`'s writes to *other* owners only commit if the whole create succeeds."
